--TEST--
A positional `#[Command]` parameter is held to the conversions an `#[Option]` is, and an `array<string>` is allowed only as the last one — `rule:tooling/commands-are-compiled` and `rule:tooling/a-parameter-is-an-argument-unless-it-is-an-option`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Cases of two different enums leave no enum for a word to be a case of,
// so no conversion exists. `float` and `?int` have none either.
enum Level {
    Quiet,
    Loud,
}

enum Mode {
    Fast,
    Slow,
}

class Radio {
    #[Core\Command(name: "tune")]
    public static function tune(Level::Loud|Mode::Fast $level): uint {
        return 0;
    }

    #[Core\Command(name: "mix")]
    public static function mix(float $gain, ?int $track, array<string> $files, string $out): uint {
        return 0;
    }
}

uint $status = Core\Command::run();
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0746]: `Level::Loud|Mode::Fast` is not a type an argument of `tune` can be given at
%A
error[E0746]: `float` is not a type an argument of `mix` can be given at
%A
error[E0746]: `int|null` is not a type an argument of `mix` can be given at
%A
error[E0746]: `$files` of `mix` is an `array<string>` and is not the last argument
%A
error: aborting due to 4 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
